actor receptor 4</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>fgfr4</italic></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">XM_344570</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.89 &#x000b1; 0.03</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.98 &#x000b1; 0.03</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tfn1-ehp0115-000909"><p>GenBank accession numbers from <xref ref-type="bibr" rid="b35-ehp0115-000909">GenBank (2007)</xref>.</p></fn><fn id="tfn2-ehp0115-000909"><label>*</label><p>Significant difference between brain stem and forebrain.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec><ref-list><title>References</title><ref id="b1-ehp0115-000909"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Abdel-Rahman</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Dechkovskaia</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Mehta-Simmons</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Guan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Khan</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name><name><surname>Abou-Donia</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Increased expression of glial fibrillary acidic protein in cerebellum and hippocampus: differential effects on neonatal brain regional acetylcholinesterase following maternal exposure to combined chlorpyrifos and nicotine</article-title><source>J Toxicol Environ Health A</source><volume>66</volume><fpage>2047</fpage><lpage>2066</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14555401</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b2-ehp0115-000909"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Aldridge</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Levin</surname><given-names>ED</given-names></name><name><surname>Seidler</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Slotkin</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005a</year><article-title>Developmental exposure of 